The SReference structure holds everything we know about one reference and the movement growing from it. The field dirMove is the key to keeping both directions in one code path. It is -1 for a movement down from a high and +1 for a movement up from a low. Multiplying a price difference by dirMove turns it into "progress in the movement direction", so the same formula serves buys and sells. The phase field drives the tracking logic: developing, opposite leg, finished or dropped. The snapshot fields store the single decision moment, including the feature vector.
