The SHistoricalObservation structure is one row of the statistical database. Besides the descriptive fields required by the specification, two fields do most of the work. The field remN stores how far price extended after the snapshot, in ATR at the snapshot. The field favN stores how far the opposite move reached, measured from the snapshot close in the same unit. Normalizing by ATR makes observations from quiet and volatile periods comparable in scale. It does not make different market regimes, sessions or news periods equivalent, which is one reason the similarity search also uses volatility, time of day and higher-timeframe context. The field completeBar is the first bar at which this observation could be known. It is our main guard against look-ahead.
