Every distribution in the system goes through the percentile function of the CStats class. It copies and sorts the sample, then interpolates linearly between the two nearest ranks. Linear interpolation matters with small samples, because it avoids large jumps in the entry, stop or target when a single observation enters or leaves the neighborhood. The same class also provides the mean, the standard deviation and a descriptive summary with the 25th, 50th, 75th and 90th percentiles, which we print in debug mode.
